  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Two paths, one dial",
      "items": [
        "Everything the tethered host sends arrives on usb0. DNS is rewritten to Pi-hole, which forwards to tor's DNSPort; all other TCP is REDIRECTed into TransPort.",
        "Nothing is masqueraded \u2014 the Pi is not a general router."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The gap this closes",
      "items": [
        "Non-DNS UDP is dropped on usb0, so QUIC cannot slip out of the hostile network the host is trying to leave. Measured: 5 of 5 datagrams to 8.8.8.8:443 dropped."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Control plane is separate",
      "items": [
        "The Config UI renders the same values into torrc, four dnsmasq files, the rules env and .env, then restarts only what changed.",
        "The Tether UI lives on the host: a browser there cannot reach 10.12.194.1 before it holds an address on the link."
      ]
    }
  ]
